{"page": 10, "width": 1600, "lines": [{"t": "phrasal verbs and do, does, and did", "x": 234, "y": 209, "w": 35, "h": 365}, {"t": "1o. Mr. Taylor attached his name to his mailbox. What did Mr. Taylor do?", "x": 280, "y": 207, "w": 1000, "h": 36}, {"t": "11. I have to remove the flat tire from my car. What do I have to do?", "x": 283, "y": 296, "w": 936, "h": 30}, {"t": "12. We didn't have any problems cooking the turkey. What did we do?", "x": 279, "y": 379, "w": 972, "h": 37}, {"t": "13. I'm removing the dirty dishes from the table. What am,I doing?", "x": 284, "y": 469, "w": 914, "h": 30}, {"t": "new product do?", "x": 340, "y": 614, "w": 236, "h": 32}, {"t": "15. Linda is trying to find her golf ball. What is Linda doing?", "x": 282, "y": 702, "w": 820, "h": 32}, {"t": "16. Susie's blue eyes aren't visible in this photo. What don't Susie's eyes do in this photo?", "x": 281, "y": 788, "w": 1204, "h": 33}, {"t": "17. Jim always forgets to place salt and pepper on the table. What does Jim always do?", "x": 281, "y": 873, "w": 1186, "h": 37}, {"t": "18. Bill didn't go to work last Friday. What didn't Bill do?", "x": 281, "y": 962, "w": 764, "h": 32}, {"t": "19. Sally returned Frank's camera. What did Sally do?", "x": 283, "y": 1051, "w": 721, "h": 30}, {"t": "2. FOCUS ON: phrasal verbs and do,does, and did", "x": 341, "y": 1313, "w": 1157, "h": 46}, {"t": "Like ordinary verbs, phrasal verbs form negatives and questions with do, does,", "x": 338, "y": 1385, "w": 1148, "h": 36}, {"t": "p!p pue", "x": 337, "y": 1424, "w": 122, "h": 37}, {"t": "Present tense questions", "x": 372, "y": 1500, "w": 368, "h": 35}, {"t": "In the present tense, questions are formed with do (except when the subject is he,", "x": 424, "y": 1548, "w": 1107, "h": 34}, {"t": "she, it, or the name of one person or thing):", "x": 423, "y": 1586, "w": 588, "h": 34}, {"t": "Why do I always fall for losers?", "x": 495, "y": 1647, "w": 412, "h": 35}, {"t": "Do you sometimes doze off in class?", "x": 493, "y": 1692, "w": 478, "h": 34}, {"t": "Do we ever give in to pressure?", "x": 491, "y": 1737, "w": 412, "h": 34}, {"t": "How do these bottle tops come off?", "x": 491, "y": 1782, "w": 470, "h": 31}, {"t": "When the subject is he, she, it, or the name of one person or thing, does is used.", "x": 421, "y": 1854, "w": 1072, "h": 36}, {"t": "Remember that the -s form of the verb is not used in questions:", "x": 420, "y": 1892, "w": 897, "h": 38}, {"t": "Does this welding torch throw sparks up into the air?", "x": 491, "y": 1956, "w": 701, "h": 34}, {"t": "Present tense negatives", "x": 367, "y": 2029, "w": 365, "h": 36}, {"t": "In the present tense, negatives are formed with do not or don't (except when the", "x": 415, "y": 2076, "w": 1097, "h": 37}, {"t": "subject is he, she, it, or the name of one person or thing):", "x": 416, "y": 2113, "w": 778, "h": 39}]}
{"page": 100, "width": 1600, "lines": [{"t": "14", "x": 269, "y": 113, "w": 105, "h": 80}, {"t": "TH E", "x": 972, "y": 119, "w": 69, "h": 24}, {"t": "participle adjectives formed from phrasal verbs, part 1", "x": 270, "y": 222, "w": 33, "h": 571}, {"t": "14. FOCUS ON: participle adjectives formed from", "x": 383, "y": 269, "w": 1117, "h": 53}, {"t": "phrasal verbs, part 1", "x": 383, "y": 328, "w": 476, "h": 53}, {"t": "The past participles of many English verbs can also be used as adjectives. You", "x": 379, "y": 400, "w": 1109, "h": 43}, {"t": "will see that sentences with adjectives formed from past participles are very simi-", "x": 378, "y": 441, "w": 1151, "h": 43}, {"t": "lar to sentences with verbs in the passive voice: in both cases a form of be is", "x": 377, "y": 482, "w": 1091, "h": 43}, {"t": "a sentence contains an adjective formed from a past participle or a verb in the", "x": 378, "y": 566, "w": 1113, "h": 41}, {"t": "passive voice:", "x": 381, "y": 609, "w": 210, "h": 36}, {"t": "The door was closed. (ls this a passive sentence or is closed an adjective?)", "x": 544, "y": 666, "w": 926, "h": 34}, {"t": "Sometimes, whether a sentence contains an adjective formed from a past partici-", "x": 382, "y": 740, "w": 1138, "h": 37}, {"t": "ple or a verb in the passive voice is clear from the sentence structure:", "x": 381, "y": 783, "w": 986, "h": 33}, {"t": "The door was closed by the secretary. (passive)", "x": 547, "y": 844, "w": 576, "h": 33}, {"t": "The door was closed when I came home last night. (adjective)", "x": 547, "y": 887, "w": 757, "h": 34}, {"t": "or the context:", "x": 383, "y": 957, "w": 221, "h": 30}, {"t": "question: What happens if the health inspector finds rats in a restaurant?", "x": 546, "y": 1018, "w": 901, "h": 31}, {"t": "answer: It's closed. (passive)", "x": 544, "y": 1060, "w": 366, "h": 33}, {"t": "question: Is the window open?", "x": 545, "y": 1130, "w": 392, "h": 37}, {"t": "answer: It's closed. (adjective)", "x": 544, "y": 1178, "w": 388, "h": 30}, {"t": "But in some cases it is not possible to say absolutely whether a sentence con-", "x": 379, "y": 1244, "w": 1094, "h": 34}, {"t": "tains an adjective formed from a past participle or a verb in the passive voice.", "x": 376, "y": 1283, "w": 1097, "h": 37}, {"t": "Fortunately, it is usually not very important because the meaning is often essen-", "x": 379, "y": 1326, "w": 1128, "h": 34}, {"t": "tially the same. For that reason, throughout this book true adjectives formed", "x": 378, "y": 1365, "w": 1088, "h": 37}, {"t": "from past participles and past participles functioning as adjectives are both", "x": 378, "y": 1406, "w": 1070, "h": 36}, {"t": "classified as participle adjectives.", "x": 380, "y": 1450, "w": 464, "h": 30}, {"t": "Much more important than the difference between adjectives formed from past", "x": 380, "y": 1532, "w": 1128, "h": 30}, {"t": "participles and past participles functioning as adjectives is what the words mean.", "x": 377, "y": 1567, "w": 1144, "h": 42}, {"t": "Some participle adjectives are written with a hyphen (make-up), some without a", "x": 378, "y": 1652, "w": 1127, "h": 36}, {"t": "hyphen (fixed up), and some as one word (rundown). Not everyone agrees which", "x": 375, "y": 1692, "w": 1130, "h": 38}, {"t": "participle adjectives should be hyphenated, which should not, and which should", "x": 376, "y": 1731, "w": 1134, "h": 41}, {"t": "be written as one word, so you will occasionally see the same participle adjective", "x": 379, "y": 1776, "w": 1135, "h": 33}, {"t": "written with or without a hyphen or written as one word. Also, British English", "x": 376, "y": 1814, "w": 1092, "h": 37}, {"t": "hyphenates many participle adjectives that are not normally hyphenated in", "x": 379, "y": 1857, "w": 1066, "h": 36}, {"t": "American English; many of the participle adjectives shown unhyphenated in this", "x": 379, "y": 1895, "w": 1127, "h": 38}, {"t": "book are hyphenated in British English.", "x": 379, "y": 1937, "w": 564, "h": 35}, {"t": "98", "x": 272, "y": 2177, "w": 32, "h": 32}]}
